    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n45931" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐχθο-δοπός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>hateful</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φώς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Ph.</u>
					1137
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πόλεμος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Ach.</u>
					226
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῖα . . ἀνεστέναζες . . ἐχθοδόπ᾽
					Ἀτρείδαις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Aj.</u>
					931
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῆς ὁδοῦ ἐχθοδοποῦ γεγονυίας πολλοῖς,
					ἴσως δὲ . . ἑτέροις προσφιλοῦς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Lg.</u>
					810d
				</span></i>
			; of a drug, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.Com.
				196
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. ὄμματα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					4.1669
				</span></i>
			. (Perh. by assimilation fr. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐχθοδαπός</span> 'foreign', 'hostile' (q.v.).)</div>
